node_modules
dist
.audit
*.log
.DS_Store
.assets-staging
.assets-backup
# Build output of scripts/build-runtime.ts. `assets/` is the committed copy.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing: a bare `runtime` is an any-depth path-segment
# rule, so it also ignores `scripts/runtime/` — the hand-written sources
# (`log.ts`, `worktree-audit.ts`, and `tests/{expect,support,fixtures}.ts`) that
# `scripts/patches.ts` imports. A fresh clone then cannot run
# `node scripts/build-runtime.ts` at all (`ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND
# scripts/runtime/tests/fixtures.ts`). Anchoring the rule to the repository root
# keeps the build output ignored while the sources stay tracked. Do not "tidy"
# this back to a bare `runtime`.
/runtime
# Upstream sources staged with RUNTIME_SOURCE_PATCHES applied, then bundled.
.runtime-sources
# Scratch space for local verification; never part of the package.
.tmp

